 | OQ-PAY-12575 | **✅ ANSWERED 2026-09-22 — THE CODE COMES FROM SETTINGS → NUMBERING, AND THE PROBLEM DISSOLVES RATHER THAN BEING SOLVED.** PO ruling, verbatim: *"(b) Put it in Settings today — DEP-260922-0001 — Settings → Numbering, like every other number"*, which SUPERSEDES the answer given minutes earlier (*"a) Add a counter — DEP-260922-CHK-01"*) because a measurement intervened: the format grammar caps a format string at **24 characters** and `DEP-{YY}{MM}{DD}-{TENDER}-{00}` is **30**. **The `deposit_batch` series already existed, already had a counter and was already seeded** — so option (b) needed no new series, no seeding and no rule change; the banking path simply ALLOCATES from it. **There is no per-day-per-tender counter to build and no retry loop to get right**: the series allocator takes a row lock and already serves thirty other numbers. **The tender leaves the code and lives in the `method` column it already had.** **BUILT 2026-09-22, `CR-135-BRC07` `P0.6`, version `2.330.0`** — `apps/payments/reconciliation._allocate_batch_code`; `batch_code` and `method_token` are deleted and the comment saying this was impossible is struck in the same commit. Seeded default is now `DEP-{YY}{MM}{DD}-{0000}` → **`DEP-260922-0001`**. ⚠ **ONE CLAUSE OF THE CLOSING ROW IS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE:** it says `{00}` with restart `never` *"reaches DEP-260922-99 and then cannot allocate at all"*. It does not — `render` never truncates and `will_overflow` is a Settings-screen WARNING, so `{00}` at 100 renders `DEP-260922-100`, unique and lawful (measured). Four digits was taken because it is the number the PO wrote; the **yearly restart** proposed in the same row was NOT taken, because its reason is the same untruth and it would put `numbering_restart_backdated` on the banking path — cutting last December's batch in January would be refused by name. ⚠ Existing tenants keep `{00}` in a row they own: reported, not migrated. — 🔒 **WHAT NUMBER DOES THE SECOND TILL OF THE DAY