 | OQ-INT-12574 | **WILL NEW WORLD ADD `ACH`, `Money order` AND `Lockbox` TO THEIR *OTHER PAYMENT TYPE* VALIDATION SET — AND IF THEY SPELL THEM DIFFERENTLY, WHAT ARE THEIR WORDS?** ⚠ **THIS IS A DEPENDENCY ON ANOTHER COMPANY, NOT A QUESTION FOR THE PO, AND IT IS THE ONE THING THAT CAN STOP THIS FEED WORKING.** New World's five `ReceiptPaymentType` values are Cash · Check · Charge · Other · Wire Transfer and **none of them is ACH**. The PO ruled on 2026-09-22 — verbatim, *"we send ACH, Moenry Order and Lockbox - as mapping from our side and wil ask them to map it at their end"* — so those three tenders go as **`3` Other** carrying a word in `ReceiptPaymentOtherType`. **Their specification says that word must match a validation set held on THEIR side.** Until their team adds the three, **every receipt carrying one is rejected at their end** — and for ACH that is most of this feed. ⚠ **NOTHING IS BLOCKED HERE AND NOTHING IS STUBBED.** The receipts are built, the words are sent, and a rejection is THEIR control working, which is this change's whole posture — *send it, let them reject it*, never withhold money from a City's books to pre-empt a check we do not own. ⚠ **AND THE ANSWER COSTS NO REBUILD WHEN IT COMES.** The three words are configuration: shipped defaults in `apps/integrations/mappings.NEWWORLD_TENDER_DEFAULTS`, overridden per tenant by an ordinary tender mapping row on the connection. A different spelling is a clerk's row, not a release. ⚠ **IN PRACTICE ONLY THE `ACH` ROW MATTERS TODAY**: this feed is `origin = webhook` only, so cash, cheque, money order and lockbox cannot appear in it at all — they are counter and post work. | external dependency (New World / Logos) | `CR-132-BRC07`, PO ruling 2026-09-22; New World import specification v2023.1.11, `ReceiptPaymentOtherType` | nothing is blocked — receipts are sent meanwhile and a rejection is visible at their end | 🔴 OPEN |
