-| OQ-PAY-12603 | **CANCEL IS PROCESSING-ONLY, AND A COUNTER CASH PAYMENT IS `cleared` THE SAME MINUTE — SO *"I JUST TOOK THAT FROM THE WRONG PERSON"* AT A WINDOW REACHES **REVERSE**, NOT CANCEL. IS THAT WHAT THE PO WANTS?** ⚠ **THIS IS A COLLISION BETWEEN TWO FRAMES OF ONE DRAWING, WHICH IS WHY IT REACHES THE PO RATHER THAN BEING SETTLED IN CODE (CLAUDE.md law 13).** ⚠ **NOTHING IS BLOCKED AND NOTHING IS STUBBED** — `POST /payments/{id}/cancel` is built, and it succeeds on `processing` and refuses `cleared` by name while pointing the clerk at Reverse, which is exactly what the phase-3 task board's `P3.13` asks for. **THE TWO FRAMES:** p044 says *"**Cancel** is for money that never cleared — the mistake is minutes old, in an open batch, and nothing has reached the bank. **Reverse** is for money that arrived and went back"*, and `US-PAY-004` §1 has said *"Cancel only while processing"* since it was signed. **But p043 draws the Cancel modal over `PMT-2609-000418`, which p035 draws as CLEARED, with a clearing date and a bill it paid off** — and its consequence box says *"$158.10 leaves Ana Alvarez's account · BL-2609-000085 re-opens at $158.10"*, which only a cleared payment can do. **B14 rule 37 settles the build** — *build the shape they agree on* — and they agree on the processing case, so that is what shipped. **WHAT IS NOT SETTLED IS THE COUNTER.** A cash payment taken at a window is recorded with a clearing date the same minute, so it is `cleared`, so Cancel refuses it — and the drawing's own scenario is *"Taken 40 minutes ago, in your open counter"*. **TWO CONSEQUENCES FOLLOW, AND THE SECOND IS THE MONEY ONE.** (1) A clerk at a counter fixing a same-minute mistake needs **Reverse**, which is `SystemAdminOnly` under `BR-PAY-1070` — so in a two-person utility the person who made the mistake cannot fix it. (2) **p050's act table gives Cancel *"a reversing pair"* in the ledger, and for the processing case there is nothing to reverse:** `record_payment` returns before the allocator when `cleared_at is None` and posts nothing, so the built cancel writes no journal line (hard rule 5 — the ledger posting service has no entry to mirror) and carries `no_entry_to_reverse_payment_never_posted` + `no_bill_reopened_payment_met_none` on every result. **THE QUESTION, IN PLAIN ENGLISH:** *when a clerk takes $158.10 in cash from the wrong person and notices forty minutes later — before the drawer is counted — should they press **Cancel** or **Reverse**?* **THREE OPTIONS: (a)** leave it as built — Cancel is processing-only, the counter case is a Reverse, and the Reverse gate stays Admin *(what is shipped)*; **(b)** widen Cancel to a cleared payment that is still in an OPEN counter batch — which means Cancel gains a ledger half and becomes a second reversal path with a different name, the exact confusion this phase exists to end; **(c)** leave Cancel alone and widen the **Reverse** gate for the same-day, same-batch case, which is a change to `BR-PAY-1070` and nobody's to make but the PO's. | product · money path (who may undo a counter mistake) | `CR-137-BRC07` `P3.2` · blueprint p043–p044 and the act table p050 · `EP-PAY-01` US-PAY-004 §1 + TC-2 · `BR-PAY-021` · `BR-PAY-1070` · `apps/payments/cancel.py` · `apps/payments/services.record_payment` · B14 rule 37 | **nothing is blocked** — cancel is built and live for the processing case, and the refusal on a cleared payment names Reverse | 🔴 **OPEN — raised 2026-09-23** |
